From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:23:28 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] selftests: apple-dcp: follow the T8132 idle runtime PM

The J713 idle power-down wraps the ATC mux callback in atcphy_rpm_get()
and atcphy_rpm_put(), brings a USB2-only PHY back through
atcphy_setup_pipehandler() after its domain was off, and gives the
dwc3-apple glue a pre_core_rpm flag.

Extract the production runtime PM wrappers next to the mux callback,
and atcphy_setup_pipehandler() where the restore calls it, and add the
idle_rpm, rpm_held and pre_core_rpm fields to the fixture structs. The
fixture PHYs and controllers are not T8132, so all three stay false: a
PHY runtime PM call would trip the existing root-port mocks or the new
pm_runtime_get_noresume() stub. No assertion changes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(backported from commit 94921e7f184bbd3291844583f181af0b86ed28d0)
[j604: on the 1.607 harness, whose dwc3_apple fixture has neither
 shutting_down nor host_only and whose lifecycle.py does not import
 firmware_lineage: the fixture gets the idle_rpm, rpm_held and
 pre_core_rpm fields the T8132 glue of this branch has, and lifecycle.py
 imports atc_restore_helpers next to the base list. With it the apple-dcp
 host suite reads 27 ok / 30 not ok, as on the base (without it 19 / 38).]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 .../selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/common.py   | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 .../drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/dwc3/mocks.c          |  2 ++
 .../drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py          |  6 +++++-
 .../selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/phy.py      |  5 ++++-
 .../selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/pm.py       |  6 +++++-
 .../drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/teardown_pm.py        |  3 ++-
 6 files changed, 35 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/common.py b/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/common.py
index 4097d7db7d..48a0edadbe 100644
--- a/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/common.py
+++ b/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/common.py
@@ -109,6 +109,23 @@ def atc_function(source, name):
     return block(source, marker.start()) + '\n' if marker else ''
 
 
+# The runtime PM wrappers of a PHY that powers down while idle (T8132 idle_power_off).
+# Fixture PHYs leave idle_rpm false, so the wrappers must not reach runtime PM; older
+# sources have none and atc_function() then yields ''.
+ATC_RPM = ('atcphy_rpm_get', 'atcphy_rpm_busy', 'atcphy_rpm_sync', 'atcphy_rpm_put')
+
+
+def atc_restore_helpers(source):
+    """What atcphy_restore_after_pd_off() needs beyond the parking helpers.
+
+    With T8132 idle runtime PM a USB2-only PHY is brought back as at probe, through
+    atcphy_setup_pipehandler(); older sources only park the PIPE. '' when unused.
+    """
+    if 'atcphy_setup_pipehandler(' not in atc_function(source, 'atcphy_restore_after_pd_off'):
+        return ''
+    return atc_function(source, 'atcphy_setup_pipehandler')
+
+
 def atc_mux_without_pm(source):
     """Lane/teardown fixtures omit USB PM, keeping mode mapping and lane work real.
 
diff --git a/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/dwc3/mocks.c b/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/dwc3/mocks.c
index 10d238b922..29006a4c34 100644
--- a/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/dwc3/mocks.c
+++ b/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/dwc3/mocks.c
@@ -77,6 +77,8 @@ struct dwc3_apple {
 	void *dev;
 	struct phy *usb2_phy, *usb3_phy;
 	bool fixed_hub, core_active, core_exit_pending, reset_pending;
+	/* T8132 only: runtime PM of an idle controller; never set here. */
+	bool idle_rpm, rpm_held, pre_core_rpm;
 	unsigned long usb2_power_off_pending, usb3_power_off_pending;
 };
 static unsigned int polls, fail_poll, reset_calls, reset_writes, core_writes;
diff --git a/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py b/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py
index 96fd0b5dce..ca30ad95a7 100644
